{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block content %}
<div class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Who we are</span>
    <h1>EAA Chapter 1699</h1>
    <p>A group of aviation enthusiasts, aircraft builders and pilots based at
       {{ site.airport.name }} who get together to share ideas, exchange
       information, encourage safety, serve the local aviation community, and
       have a great deal of fun doing so.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        The Experimental Aircraft Association has been the home of homebuilders,
        restorers and grassroots aviation since 1953. Chapters are the local
        expression of that — and Chapter 1699 is the one at
        {{ site.airport.name }} ({{ site.airport.ident }}) in
        {{ site.airport.city }}, New York.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are a 501(c)(3) non-profit, run entirely by volunteers. Nobody here
        gets paid. What people get instead is a hangar full of second opinions,
        a tool locker they did not have to fund alone, and a standing invitation
        to somebody else's first-flight day.
      </p>

      <h2>What actually happens here</h2>
      <h3>Technical Counselors</h3>
      <p>
        EAA-trained members who visit your project in person — at any stage,
        for free — and give you an honest assessment. Builders who use a
        Technical Counselor have a measurably better safety record. That is the
        whole pitch.
      </p>

      <h3>Flight Advisors</h3>
      <p>
        Before the first flight of a newly built or newly restored aircraft,
        a Flight Advisor helps you look squarely at the aircraft, the
        conditions, and — the hard one — your own currency and proficiency.
      </p>

      <h3>IMC and VMC Clubs</h3>
      <p>
        Monthly scenario-based sessions. IMC Club works instrument scenarios;
        VMC Club works the visual-flying decisions that quietly kill people.
        Everyone in the room votes, then argues about it. Bring your opinions.
      </p>

      <h3>Young Eagles</h3>
      <p>
        Free first flights for kids aged 8 to 17, flown by volunteer chapter
        pilots. More than two million kids have flown in the programme since
        1992. Some of them are now our members.
      </p>

      <h3>Ray Aviation Scholarship</h3>
      <p>
        Through the Ray Foundation, chapters can fund a young person's flight
        training all the way to a certificate. It is the single biggest thing a
        chapter this size can do for aviation's future.
      </p>

      <h3>Members' projects</h3>
      <p>
        The reason to come to a meeting. Somebody always has an update, a
        problem, a photo of something that arrived in the mail, or a wing that
        is now, at long last, closed up.
      </p>

      <h2>Visiting</h2>
      <p>
        Fly in or drive in — both are equally welcome, and roughly half of
        every breakfast crowd arrives by road. If you are flying in, check
        {{ site.airport.ident }} in your favourite app for current field
        conditions; it is a working grass-and-asphalt field, not an airline
        hub, and it rewards a pass overhead before you commit.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are driving, put
        <strong>{{ site.airport.street }}, {{ site.airport.city }}, {{ site.airport.state }} {{ site.airport.zip }}</strong>
        into your phone and follow it to the end.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="sidebar">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3>Home field</h3>
          <ul class="factlist" style="margin-top:1rem">
            <li><span class="label">Airport</span><span>{{ site.airport.name }}</span></li>
            <li><span class="label">Ident</span><span class="mono">{{ site.airport.ident }}</span></li>
            <li><span class="label">Runway</span><span>{{ site.airport.runway }}</span></li>
            <li><span class="label">Fuel</span><span>{{ site.airport.fuel }}</span></li>
            <li><span class="label">Address</span><span>{{ site.airport.street }}<br>{{ site.airport.city }}, {{ site.airport.state }} {{ site.airport.zip }}</span></li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn btn-outline btn-block btn-sm" href="{{ site.airport | maplink }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open in maps</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3>Interested in joining?</h3>
          <p class="small muted">
            Come to something first — a breakfast, a meeting, whatever is next
            on the calendar. Membership makes far more sense once you have put
            faces to it.
          </p>
          <a class="btn btn-primary btn-block btn-sm" href="{{ '/contact' | url }}">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3>Non-profit status</h3>
          <p class="small muted">
            EAA Chapter 1699, Inc. is a registered 501(c)(3) charitable
            organisation in {{ site.airport.city }}, NY.<br>
            EIN <span class="mono">{{ site.ein }}</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
